That ordinance had several enforcement methods including prosecution in the municipal court,

1643
01:07:15,200 --> 01:07:19,840
stop work orders, in other words if they fail to do what they're supposed to do we can issue

1644
01:07:19,840 --> 01:07:25,400
a stop work order on other things that the communication companies are doing and permit

1645
01:07:25,400 --> 01:07:30,560
revocation for instance if they get a permit to do some of this.

1646
01:07:30,560 --> 01:07:37,440
These all are effective to some degree but they are also ineffective.

1647
01:07:37,440 --> 01:07:44,600
For instance in municipal court they're just not equipped for instance to cite and potentially

1648
01:07:44,600 --> 01:07:51,400
jail or whatever a corporation like AT&T, they're used to dealing with individuals.

1649
01:07:51,400 --> 01:07:55,960
So that turns out not to be a very effective method for us.

1650
01:07:55,960 --> 01:08:01,440
Stop work orders are not effective if they don't have any work order ongoing at the time

1651
01:08:01,440 --> 01:08:07,420
and permit revocation again is only effective when they're trying to obtain a revocation.

1652
01:08:07,420 --> 01:08:11,720
So those methods have some lack of effectiveness.

1653
01:08:11,720 --> 01:08:19,400
A more effective method that we've been utilizing and a more informal one has been to develop

1654
01:08:19,400 --> 01:08:24,480
a more cooperative relationship with our communication providers.

1655
01:08:24,480 --> 01:08:30,640
Our city ITS department is spearheading that effort and they're making a very coordinated

1656
01:08:30,640 --> 01:08:38,880
effort through our C-Click fix and other communications with the city to address each of those and

1657
01:08:38,880 --> 01:08:44,800
to get with those providers to address citizen complaints in a timely fashion.

1658
01:08:44,800 --> 01:08:51,960
Admittedly we don't always get the quick results that we would like to have but it is an effort

1659
01:08:51,960 --> 01:08:57,180
that does produce fruit from time to time and we continue to do it but once again the

1660
01:08:57,180 --> 01:09:05,400
problem is somewhat immense and there's not the manpower to address this as we would like.

1661
01:09:05,400 --> 01:09:11,840
Contractors have largely been responsive but they also don't necessarily have the resources

1662
01:09:11,840 --> 01:09:18,840
on hand to address the magnitude of the problems that exist and oftentimes their work is done

1663
01:09:18,840 --> 01:09:22,600
through third party contractors as well.

1664
01:09:22,600 --> 01:09:27,480
So this has been a frustrating experience for the city as well.

1665
01:09:27,480 --> 01:09:35,040
As a city attorney my job is to evaluate these tools that we have and try to address these

1666
01:09:35,040 --> 01:09:40,280
problems in as effective a manner as we can.

1667
01:09:40,280 --> 01:09:46,120
Frankly as we discussed all those tools are not available to us in all situations such

1668
01:09:46,120 --> 01:09:52,000
as I indicated when we're in the municipal court and we're not dealing with an individual

1669
01:09:52,000 --> 01:09:55,400
and sometimes the bang is not worth the buck.

1670
01:09:55,400 --> 01:10:01,600
In other words the expense involved with pursuing a remedy that would be effective is more expensive

1671
01:10:01,600 --> 01:10:03,520
than necessary.

1672
01:10:03,520 --> 01:10:12,080
But we have a methodology that when compliance arises to a certain level such as when public

1673
01:10:12,080 --> 01:10:19,440
safety is implicated or when there are repeat violations of our ordinances that we can seek

1674
01:10:19,440 --> 01:10:24,000
to obtain what's called injunctive relief through the circuit court.

1675
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,160
That is a relief or a methodology that we've used in other areas and we are exploring it

1676
01:10:30,160 --> 01:10:33,720
at this time and we will continue to do so.

1677
01:10:33,720 --> 01:10:41,280
We ask for the continued patience of the citizens as we work to solve this thorny problem and

1678
01:10:41,280 --> 01:10:47,640
it's a difficult problem but we're doing the best we can and we'll try to do better.

