01:38:44,180 --> 01:38:49,580
by and among the City of Huntsville and Madison County, Alabama as landlord and EE Gemini

2273
01:38:49,580 --> 01:38:55,420
Solar LLC as tenant and authorizing Mayor to sign additional documents related there

2274
01:38:55,420 --> 01:38:56,420
to.

2275
01:38:56,420 --> 01:38:57,420
Motion to approve.

2276
01:38:57,420 --> 01:38:58,420
Motion from Mr. Mayor.

2277
01:38:58,420 --> 01:38:59,420
Second.

2278
01:38:59,420 --> 01:39:00,420
Second from Mr. Kling.

2279
01:39:00,420 --> 01:39:01,420
Mr. Davis.

2280
01:39:01,420 --> 01:39:02,900
Good evening, Council Mayor.

2281
01:39:02,900 --> 01:39:04,180
Thank you, Madam President.

2282
01:39:04,180 --> 01:39:10,780
So tonight what we bring you is a tripartite agreement, really a quad-party agreement between

2283
01:39:10,780 --> 01:39:19,220
the City of Huntsville, Madison County Commission, Huntsville Utilities, and URUS, Inc., or Gemini

2284
01:39:19,220 --> 01:39:21,500
Solar LLC.

2285
01:39:21,500 --> 01:39:25,820
So what I wanted to bring you is a vicinity map, as you can see on the screen.

2286
01:39:25,820 --> 01:39:31,280
The pink square there is near the intersection of 6th Street and Wall Trana.

2287
01:39:31,280 --> 01:39:36,500
So that is property that has been on for probably 30 plus years.

2288
01:39:36,500 --> 01:39:41,300
It's jointly on between the City of Huntsville and the Madison County Commission.

2289
01:39:41,300 --> 01:39:48,420
It was purchased many years ago as a potential industrial site or for industrial use to benefit

2290
01:39:48,420 --> 01:39:52,060
the holistic community, meaning City of Huntsville and Madison County.

2291
01:39:52,060 --> 01:39:56,180
I want to go through some details of this lease agreement.

2292
01:39:56,180 --> 01:40:01,260
The County Commission passed the same document that's before you tonight earlier this week.

2293
01:40:01,260 --> 01:40:06,220
So what we would do in partnership with Madison County and Huntsville Utilities is enter into

2294
01:40:06,220 --> 01:40:11,780
a ground lease, so we're not selling the property, the public remains the owners of the property,

2295
01:40:11,780 --> 01:40:19,300
of 237 acres to generate a new 40 megawatt solar facility, very significant local power

2296
01:40:19,300 --> 01:40:23,900
generation in a very green manner.

2297
01:40:23,900 --> 01:40:26,180
The lease term would be for 35 years.

2298
01:40:26,180 --> 01:40:30,500
At the end of that term, we would have two options, you know, a future council and a

2299
01:40:30,500 --> 01:40:35,260
future County Commission could renew and extend and continue to generate power there.

2300
01:40:35,260 --> 01:40:41,340
If we chose not to do so, all the solar facility that would be on the property would have to

2301
