be removed and the property returned to its natural state.

2302
01:40:46,160 --> 01:40:49,140
So there is a revenue stream attached to that.

2303
01:40:49,140 --> 01:40:55,180
So should you approve this tonight, they'll start their due diligence period and then

2304
01:40:55,180 --> 01:40:58,860
get into what we refer to as a development period.

2305
01:40:58,860 --> 01:41:02,100
That's actual construction in this document, we see development period.

2306
01:41:02,100 --> 01:41:07,340
So once construction starts, they have 14 months to complete and be generating power.

2307
01:41:07,340 --> 01:41:14,140
So we, during that construction period, have asked for a partial payment of the annual

2308
01:41:14,140 --> 01:41:21,540
lease in the amount of $23,796 and then upon completion and it generating power, there

2309
01:41:21,540 --> 01:41:26,940
is an annual lease payment of $237,690 per year.

2310
01:41:26,940 --> 01:41:30,780
We will split those proceeds 50-50 with a county.

2311
01:41:30,780 --> 01:41:35,780
Huntsville utilities is here tonight, who is the backbone of this project.

2312
01:41:35,780 --> 01:41:40,020
So if you would like to know more about the solar and its generation and how it comes

2313
01:41:40,020 --> 01:41:46,340
onto our grid, I can tell you from where I sit in City Hall of Industrial Development

2314
01:41:46,340 --> 01:41:55,340
and Economic Development and some of the long-term goals that TVA is working on and people like

2315
01:41:55,340 --> 01:42:01,940
Eli Lilly coming in and Space Command and the growth of the FBI and Redstone Arsenal,

2316
01:42:01,940 --> 01:42:08,980
the proximity to our grid in Redstone Arsenal, this is a great solution for our community,

2317
01:42:08,980 --> 01:42:14,820
especially not only for the next 35 years, but there's about a three to five year window

2318
01:42:14,820 --> 01:42:20,860
where adding this local generation to our overall power grid helps strengthen this community

2319
01:42:20,860 --> 01:42:26,940
as far as our future and continued growth and being able to manage that and manage cost.

2320
01:42:26,940 --> 01:42:32,420
I think Wes Kelly, when he come for this council, talked about the five goals and one of those

2321
01:42:32,420 --> 01:42:35,900
was local power generation, which keeps our rates low.

2322
01:42:35,900 --> 01:42:37,240
This is a prime example of that.

2323
01:42:37,240 --> 01:42:42,180
So I'll defer, answer any questions you have about the lease, but as far as the project,

2324
01:42:42,180 --> 01:42:44,180
Chris Jones is here with Huntsville Utilities.

2325
01:42:44,180 --> 01:42:45,740
Questions, Mr. Mayor.

2326
