We will now hear from Liliana Painter. She is our concluding speaker.

2831
02:16:15,980 --> 02:16:18,980
Good evening council members.

2832
02:16:18,980 --> 02:16:20,980
My name is Liliana Painter.

2833
02:16:20,980 --> 02:16:22,980
My address is correct on this sheet.

2834
02:16:22,980 --> 02:16:27,980
I'm a Huntsville resident, a working mom and a small business owner.

2835
02:16:27,980 --> 02:16:33,980
First, I want to express gratitude for the detailed meeting we had two weeks ago.

2836
02:16:33,980 --> 02:16:41,980
The presentations resolutions and initiatives discussed show a clear effort to ensure that residents feel heard.

2837
02:16:41,980 --> 02:16:47,980
And that is something I truly value and want to see continued.

2838
02:16:47,980 --> 02:16:59,980
At the same time, the length of the meeting highlighted an opportunity to improve consistency, efficiency and transparency and how we address those concerns moving forward.

2839
02:16:59,980 --> 02:17:23,980
I also want to acknowledge the Mayor's Office and the many initiatives, organizations and community events that continue to bring Huntsville together. Programs like the Civic Engagement Academy, the Citizens Police Academy are important investments that help our residents better understand how our city operates.

2840
02:17:23,980 --> 02:17:35,980
However, we are beginning to see signs of growth that is outpacing capacity across our public systems.

2841
02:17:35,980 --> 02:17:45,980
From what is visible, departments like this, like the Multicultural Affairs Office, appear to be carrying a growing scope of work with limited staffing.

2842
02:17:45,980 --> 02:17:55,980
Similarly, with public safety programs, there are essential functions that rely heavily on volunteer support.

2843
02:17:55,980 --> 02:18:00,980
Because when systems are strained, residents feel it.

2844
02:18:00,980 --> 02:18:07,980
Whether that's in access to services, response times or overall quality of life.

2845
02:18:07,980 --> 02:18:22,980
So my question is, how are we planning ahead to ensure public service workforce has the capacity to support and structure needed to keep up with that growth?

2846
02:18:22,980 --> 02:18:32,980
Planning ahead and investing in capacity also ensures Huntsville remains a place where both residents and small businesses can continue to grow with confidence.

2847
02:18:32,980 --> 02:18:39,980
Lastly, how are the boards currently being incorporated into the planning process?

2848
02:18:39,980 --> 02:18:51,980
And how are there opportunities to engage them earlier so that residents input is reflected before those decisions are finalized?

2849
02:18:51,980 --> 02:18:56,980
As Huntsville grows, we have an opportunity to grow with intention.

2850
02:18:56,980 --> 02:18:59,980
And I'll give you back your time. Thank you.

2851
02:18:59,980 --> 02:19:03,980
Thank you very much. Mr. Painter is our concluding speaker.

2852
02:19:03,980 --> 02:19:07,980
Is there any other business to come before the council?

2853
02:19:07,980 --> 02:19:30,980
Seeing none, we are adjourned. Thank you, Mr. Little.
